meta {
  name: Access groups - Add a member
  type: http
  seq: 79
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/nswswk8w8wso0ko8owwk8k0w/access-groups/<group cuid>/members
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "ada@example.com"
  }
}

docs {
  Adds a member of the community to the group (#1241), named by exactly one of member (user cuid), username or email. Adding a member twice changes nothing, so a sync from another system can send its list again. Owner, admins, moderators with the manage members right. Token ability: groups:write. Only the owner and the admins add by email: a moderator adds by member or username, and a request by email gets 403 (a token follows the role of its account).

  With email, the answer is 204 with no body, whether a member of the community has the address or not (nothing is added then): the answer never tells who has an address. Read the members of the group to know who is in it.

  With member or username, the answer is 200 with the member, and someone who is not a member of the community gives a validation issue (400).

  The add and the remove of a group member share a limit of 10 requests a minute for each account: 429 after it.
}
